#heading(numbering: none)[Introduction]

Every book starts with a promise to the reader. Use the introduction to say
who this book is for, what they will be able to do or understand by the end,
and why you are the person to take them there.

Keep it short. Readers decide in the first few pages whether to keep going,
so lead with the problem they have, not with your background.
